That's right. Though if I had given a yet more complete description it
would have not been a possible solution in this case; I neither opened
or locked the door nor had I been in that room (or at the door) before.
I didn't mention the last point in my original question.

The interesting thing with such puzzles is, IMO, that ones mind wanders
and you get very interesting solutions, even if they are not applicable
in the specific case. I like the polymorph to ooze solution.

The described situation (and thus the puzzle), BTW, did happen just by
accident; one of the barracks had still its door intact, so I skipped
it (was kind of boring, just to get a few more wands). But after coming
back to that level the third or fourth time, now equipped with ESP and
the three pets, I asked myself whether it might be possible at all to
kill the soldiers from afar without touching them myself; and tried it
that way.

The imagination of opening the door and no inhabitants visible reminded
me on some other not nethack/computer/game related puzzles of the type:
"You enter a room, everywhere dead persons lying around. What happened?"
Then you have to ask questions (concerning their wounds, the room, etc.)
to solve it. The key in this interactive puzzle is to determined the type
of the room and where it is located.

